# ── WHY THIS FILE EXISTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vercel turns EVERY .js file under api/ into its own Serverless Function. Not
# just the request handlers — every file. api/ also holds the pure modules the
# handlers require (bprCircuit, bprFormat, partsOrderForm, sheetSanity) and, up
# to now, their unit tests, so the deployment was building thirteen functions
# where four are real endpoints and five were test files.
#
# Thirteen is one over the Hobby plan's limit of twelve. Every deployment after
# api/sheetSanity.js and its test landed — which took the count from eleven to
# thirteen — failed at "Deploying outputs", AFTER a completely healthy build.
# The build log showed vite finishing in 3.77s and dist written, so the failure
# read as unrelated to the code, and production quietly went on serving an
# older build while a day of merges piled up behind it.
#
# Excluding the tests takes it from thirteen to eight. api/*.test.js is dev
# tooling; it has no business being uploaded, let alone deployed.
#
# Guarded by api/functionCount.test.js, which fails the suite before a push can
# repeat this.

*.test.js
test/

# Never uploaded, and large: the local build output and the dev-only vitest
# config are of no use to a deployment.
dist/
vitest.config.js
